# Drafted by Gemini (R25 vagrant), edited.

~ start
Narrator: A quiet stillness settles over the cobbles of the Round, with the smell of woodsmoke hanging where the dry leaves have been swept neat over fresh graves.
old_rusty [weary]: Ash on the wind and soot on the stone, the iron horse comes when the fog is full grown.
old_rusty [neutral]: It waits on the siding while crooked moon shines, so mend what needs mending and tie up your lines.
set ep_started
quest ep_the_last_ride loose_ends
if not flag.ep_fair_open
set ep_fair_open
quest ep_fair_on_the_round open
endif
* Ask about the graves -> graves
* Ask about the station -> station
* That is all -> END

~ graves
old_rusty [sad]: Lord and lady, leaf and bough, all laid under the cold turf now. Names in the granite, quiet and deep, paying the price for the peace that we keep.
-> start_menu

~ station
old_rusty [neutral]: Past the south bridge where the river-mist clings, where the rusted rail ends and the night-fiddle sings. Follow the fog where it settles Down-low, that is the way that the travellers go.
-> start_menu

~ start_menu
old_rusty [weary]: Broom in the hand and dust on the shoe. Speak if you will, while the night is still through.
* Ask about the graves -> graves
* Ask about the station -> station
* That is all -> END
